    "result_text": "Build is green. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded a duplicate-email rejection (409) to the create-owner pipeline, mirroring the existing telephone-uniqueness pattern:\n\n1. **`EnsureUniqueOwnerEmail.java`** \u2014 a new function step that reads the validated `OwnerFieldsDto` (`@Val`), and if it carries an email, compares its lower-cased form against every existing owner's email, throwing `DuplicateOwnerEmailException` on a match. Requests without an email pass through untouched.\n\n2. **`DuplicateOwnerEmailException.java`** \u2014 a checked exception (so it appears in the `throws` clause and is routed to an escalation handler).\n\n3. **`DuplicateOwnerEmailExceptionHandler.java`** \u2014 responds `409 Conflict` with `{\"errors\":[\"email\"]}`, matching the telephone handler's shape.\n\n4. **Escalation YAML** (`...DuplicateOwnerEmailException.yml`) \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted the `ensureUniqueEmail` step (governed by `transaction`, like its neighbors) between the telephone and household uniqueness checks.\n\nEmail is already lower-cased earlier by `ValidateOwnerFields`/`OwnerEmail.normalize`, so the check operates on normalized values. The acceptance test `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` and the full suite pass.",
